            <ArticleTitle>Synthesis and evaluation of 3-amino-6-aryl-pyridazines as selective CB(2) agonists for the treatment of inflammatory pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>465-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.bmcl.2009.11.117</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A series of 3-amino-6-aryl-pyridazines have been identified as CB(2) agonists with high efficacy and selectivity against the CB(1) receptor. Details of the investigation of structure-activity relationships (SAR) are disclosed, which led to the identification of pyridazine analogue 35, a compound with high potency in an in vivo model of inflammatory pain.</AbstractText>
